From d8e371d562d3c9c991ba1761a4dbb8c9d3789612 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 22:16:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 22/58] generate: STRATA_TRACE times a batch admission's phases

One stderr line per batch admission ("strata trace: admission of slot N: ...")
splits it into the drain before BGEN, the prompt (batched read, header windows,
the checkpoints' device syncs, copies into RAM and eviction, the rest), the first
window, the slot copy, freeing the slot's old state and the copy of the turn
checkpoint into the slot. Each checkpoint gets its own line, and with pipelined
groups "first rows N ms after the admission" times the refill after BADM. A drain
for another line says how many groups were in flight and what it cost.

Only with STRATA_TRACE set; without it the log and the tokens are unchanged.

Measured (4x RTX 3090, split 12,24,36, 16 slots in 4 groups, 24 admissions):
drain 25-26, header windows 23.5, checkpoint 17.3 (sync 0.1, save 17.2), first
window 11.5, slot copy 1.3, slot freed 0.0, checkpoint copy 7.8 (60 on a slot's
first fill), refill after BADM 23.7 ms.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
